      "guided_eligible": true,
      "exact_quote_texts": [
        "Out of Control\nAt this stage, the wildfire is spreading or is anticipated to spread beyond the current perimeter, or control line. In this case, BC Wildfire Service applies more aggressive suppression and control methods such as establishing control lines, burn-offs, dropping water, foam or retardant.",
        "Being Held\nAt this stage, the wildfire is projected, based on fuel and weather conditions and resource availability, to remain within the current perimeter, control line or boundary. At this point, crews may finish establishing control lines, conduct fuel management activities and mop-up (extinguishing a fire after it has been brought under control).",
        "Under Control\nAt this stage, the wildfire is not projected to spread beyond the current perimeter. BC Wildfire Service may continue to patrol the fire and extinguish hot spots while moving gear, equipment and personnel to another incident."
      ]
